 \emph{Remaining parameters.}
 Conditional on the relative valuation parameter \(\psi\), the noise parameter \(\sigma_u\), and the observability parameters \(\beta^O_z\) and \(\gamma^O_z\), the remaining take-up parameters are identified through the take-up likelihood. The distance cost coefficient \(\delta\) is identified by distance induced variation in take-up. The social image weight \(\lambda\) is identified on the normalized latent utility scale by how take-up varies with estimated observability across item/signal arms and distances. The arm specific non social payoff coefficients \(\beta_z\) are identified by residual take-up differences across item/signal arms, subject to the bracelet versus calendar relative valuation restriction.
