 The parameters \(\rho\) and \(\sigma_u\) require additional regularization. The parameter \(\rho\) maps monetary values from the relative valuation exercise into the latent utility units of the take-up model. Because this scale conversion is weakly disciplined by the data, we use a positive regularizing prior. The parameter \(\sigma_u\) governs how noisy deworming choices are as signals of intrinsic motivation. We use an inverse Gamma prior to keep this scale parameter away from degenerate values near zero. Prior predictive checks, described in Section~\ref{structural}, assess whether these priors mechanically impose the posterior patterns.
 
